isoning while repairing the  ship so it can get to safety  of course it was a heartbreaking moment  for everyone especially kirk  live long  and prosper spock then gets a full  funeral with his coffin launched into  space which seems about as  final a death as you could ask for not  so fast  in star trek 3 the search for spock we  learned that spock's body landed on the  new planet formed by the genesis device  his consciousness however has been  transferred to dr mccoy  so the enterprise crew has to save spock  from the collapsing planet and reunite  his mind  and body you won't be shocked to learn  that their mission was successful  bringing spock fully back to life by the  movie's end  alien 3 is one of the most divisive  movies in the series  but if there's one thing its detractors  and defenders agree on it's a cruel grim  piece of work the only disagreement is  whether that's good or bad  this mean streak carries to the end when  ripley burns herself alive to destroy  the alien gestating inside her before an  evil corporation can weaponize it  this ending feels like director david  fincher's attempt to make sure both  ripley  and the franchise were good and dead  forever  as we all know that didn't work five  years later ripley was back thanks to  cloning in the appropriately titled  alien resurrection  hey i thought you were dead yeah i get  that a lot  but she isn't quite the ripley we knew  her dna has been combined with the  creatures  and weaver's bug-eyed emotionless  performance feels truly alien  director jean-pierre jannu handles the  resurrection with the same dark humor  and surreal touches he'd shown off in  his earlier films such as the city of  lost children  a scene in which ripley discovers the  grotesquely mangled clones who preceded  her is particularly memorable  there's definitely a cynical meta joke  to ripley being brought back by greedy  creeps who refuse to let her die  just so they can squeeze more money out  of her but how you feel ab